WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.675
Unit 2 starts with what
the guide leaves to you.

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:07.155
The guide says the digest goes to
the owners, but owners read a page,

3
00:00:07.155 --> 00:00:11.138
not a JSON file, so the kit
writes a page and a spreadsheet.

4
00:00:11.138 --> 00:00:13.687
It says every run is in the evidence,

5
00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:18.874
but a folder of files can be changed
after the fact, so the kit checks each

6
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:24.237
run folder against its manifest, copies
it, and records every file's SHA-256.

7
00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:26.644
It lists controls and K S I's per gate,

8
00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:31.539
but someone has to say which run
supports which, so each record names its

9
00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:36.351
steps and their controls and K S I's,
from the kit's requirements catalog.

10
00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:41.202
Records are kept over time, but a record
removed from the middle goes unnoticed,

11
00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:44.412
so each record holds the hash
of the record before it.

12
00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:46.432
And the guide asks for a go/no-go,

13
00:00:46.432 --> 00:00:50.551
which raises the question of
which steps still lack evidence.

14
00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:53.275
The stage check answers it, step by step.

15
00:00:53.275 --> 00:00:58.300
The workbook's verdict: a list of files
isn't evidence until someone can check it.
